// std.lookup — partial-map application at a single key (1 + V).
//
// Ontological grounding: `dsl/std/algebra.dag` models `Map<K,V>` as
// `K -> (1 + V)`; applying the map at one key yields either absence
// (`Missing`) or a found value (`Found`). This is the shared carrier
// for every lens-local `MissingX | FoundX(T)` pair that only differed
// in label noise — see docs/thesis/compiler-std-consolidation.md
// (primary ratchet: strict two-variant Lookup pattern).
//
// Bootstrap staging: `src/v3/std/` until the v2 firewall dissolves and
// `dsl/std/` subsumes v3 std (same gate as `std.list` / `std.algebra`).
//
// `miss_int_lookup` / `hit_int_lookup` are Int-monomorphized helpers
// (v3 infer does not yet close generic `miss_lookup<value>` /
// `hit_lookup<value>` with body `Miss` / `Hit(v)`). Rust lens emission
// treats these two callables as `Lookup::Miss` / `Lookup::Hit` (see
// `emit_rust_target::render_general_callable`).

module v3.std.lookup

import std.types { Int }

// Coproduct dissolution (docs/modeling-discipline.md §4). `Lookup<value>` is
// the **1 + V** optional-presence sum for a single key read (see file header:
// `Map` at one key is `K -> (1 + V)` in `dsl/std/algebra.dag`). Classification:
// **🟢 TERMINAL (GREEN).** Four-pattern ledger — each pattern *attempted*; none
// dissolves this carrier into a different substrate shape (terminal justified):
//   1. Fact placement — Fails: `Miss` and `Hit` are not duplicative facts stashed
//      at unrelated DAG sites; they are the exclusive outcomes of *one* partial
//      read. Splitting would break the `1 + V` algebra (see THESIS.md structural
//      decompression — this is the irreducible sum for optional value).
//   2. Variant-is-data — Fails: `Miss` (unit) and `Hit(value)` (payload) are not
//      the same record with a tag field; merging would erase the empty vs. typed
//      distinction.
//   3. Algebraic form — Fails to collapse *further:* this declaration **is** the
//      shared `std` carrier for the strict two-variant lookup pattern (P2
//      single authority for `Missing|Found(T)`-shaped lenses — compiler-std
//      consolidation, `docs/thesis/compiler-std-consolidation.md`); it is not a
//      parallel enum beside a richer `std/` type.
//   4. Dimensional — Fails: absence vs. presence of `value` is a single binary
//      sum, not a product of independent dimensions to factor into fields.
//
// **Dissolution / migration receipt (compiler–std consolidation).** The first
// migrated lens that *consumes* this file (not a parallel `Missing/Found` lens
// carrier) is `src/v3/lenses/complexity.dag` — `import v3.std.lookup { Lookup, … }`
// and `cost_of` → `Lookup<Int>`. `src/v3/compiler/src/lens_cost_generated.rs` is
// the **generated** consumer at the Rust lens boundary (regen_lens; committed).
//
// **Structural consumer (P2 / INVARIANTS.md P2: declaration + realization +
// generated proof).** `Lookup` is not declaration-only:
//   - `src/v3/lenses/complexity.dag` — `cost_of` and helpers return `Lookup<Int>`;
//   - `src/v3/compiler/src/lens_cost_generated.rs` — `regen_lens` / `emit_rust_module`
//     output; the compiler includes this module and pattern-matches `Lookup` at
//     the lens boundary;
//   - `src/v3/spec/rust.dag` — `rust_lookup_instantiation` projects the carrier
//     to Rust `Lookup<i64>` for emit (Miss/Hit).

// Generic sum: one authority for “absent vs present” at a typed value.
// Variant labels `Miss` / `Hit` mirror the thesis `Missing | Found(T)` naming.
type Lookup<value>
  = Miss
  | Hit(value)

fn miss_int_lookup() -> Lookup<Int> {
  Miss
}

fn hit_int_lookup(n: Int) -> Lookup<Int> {
  Hit(n)
}
